  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Profiles
  </title>
  <p>
    Profiles are named collections of Orca settings for different activities. Orca normally
    starts with the "Default" profile. To start with another saved profile, run <code>orca -p NAME</code> or <code>orca --profile NAME</code>, replacing NAME with
    the profile's name. If Orca is already running as an application, add <code>--replace</code>.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-profiles">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Profiles</gui> category.
    </p>
    <p>
      In application preferences, select an existing profile to configure that application for
      the selected profile. For example, select a work profile to save Writer-specific settings
      for it. Selecting a profile also changes Orca's active profile. Create, rename, and remove
      profiles in the global Preferences window.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>New Profile</gui>: Creates a profile from
          the current profile's saved settings and switches to it. Type a unique name and
          confirm. Apply recent edits first if you want them included: unsaved changes are not
          copied and are discarded if you continue.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Current Profile</gui>: Select a profile to
          activate it, then adjust settings in the other categories and save your changes. Save
          any edits before switching; unsaved changes to the previous profile are discarded.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Rename...</gui>: Changes the selected
              profile's name. Use Tab to reach the button, enter a new name, and confirm it in
              the rename dialog. Then apply or save the change in the Preferences window. The
              default profile cannot be renamed.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Remove Profile...</gui>: Deletes the
              selected profile and its saved settings immediately after confirmation. If it is
              active, Orca switches to the default profile. The default profile cannot be
              removed.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
  <section id="commands-profiles">
